<title>TURKEY: TURKISH AIRLINES 1H NET PROFIT SOARS.</title>
<headline>TURKISH AIRLINES 1H NET PROFIT SOARS.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>January-June final</p>
<p>(billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>    Per shares profit (lira)	 400.99 vs    112.05</p>
<p>    Net profit			 4,009.93 vs    616.27</p>
<p>    Net sales			 42,230.29 vs 22,123.62</p>
<p>    Operating profits		2,911.00 vs  1,244.33</p>
<p>    Exceptional income	     3,999.68 vs  1,075.47</p>
<p>    Exceptional expense	    1,603.52 vs    863.99</p>
<p>    Interest paid		    1,502.47 vs  1,022.60</p>
<p>    Extraordinary income	   2,814.89 vs    824.03</p>
<p>    Extraordinary expense	  1,484.32 vs    640.96</p>
<p>    Total debts		     24,915.51 vs 17,497.42</p>
<p>    Equity			    28,581.78 vs 13,871.79</p>
<p>    Capital			   10,000.00 vs  5,500.00</p>
<p>NOTE - National carrier Turkish Airlines (THY) is in the government's privatisation programme with 98.2 percent of its capital held by the privatisation office. -- Istanbul Newsroom +90-212-2750875</p>
</text>
